## Preliminary Findings

All findings marked (unverified) are based on search snippets and require full page verification.

### Dimension 6: Enterprise IdP Integration

#### Keycloak/RHBK Integration

**fastapi-keycloak library** (unverified)
- Projects goal is to ease the integration of Keycloak (OpenID Connect) with Python, especially FastAPI
- Enables verification of identities and roles of users with Keycloak without writing additional code
- Provides OIDCUser class for dependency injection with role access via user.roles
- get_current_user() method accepts required_roles parameter for endpoint-level RBAC
- Supports password and authorization_code OAuth2 flows
- Documentation at https://fastapi-keycloak.code-specialist.com/

**fastapi-keycloak-middleware library** (unverified)
- Middleware-based alternative to fastapi-keycloak
- Supports OIDC and validates access tokens
- Reads roles and supports basic authentication
- Documentation at https://fastapi-keycloak-middleware.readthedocs.io/

**python-keycloak library maintenance status** (unverified)
- Actively maintained with releases v7.1.1 (Feb 15, 2026), v7.1.0 (Feb 13, 2026), v7.0.3 (Jan 28, 2026)
- Maintenance status: Healthy (per Snyk analysis)
- Positive version release cadence with at least one new version in the past 3 months
- No known security vulnerabilities (Snyk scan)
- Supports Keycloak's 5 latest major versions
- Only supports Python versions with active or security support by the PSF

**Keycloak OIDC discovery endpoint structure** (unverified)
- Discovery endpoint pattern: `https://keycloak-server/realms/{realm-name}/.well-known/openid-configuration`
- token_endpoint pattern: `http://localhost:8181/realms/{realm-name}/protocol/openid-connect/token`
- jwks_uri pattern: `http://localhost:8181/realms/{realm-name}/protocol/openid-connect/certs`
- Base path for endpoints: `/realms/{realm-name}/protocol/openid-connect/`
- Certificate endpoint returns public keys encoded as JSON Web Key (JWK)

**RHBK-specific endpoint patterns** (unverified)
- RHBK servers with /auth context path: `https://rhbk.example.com:8443/auth/realms/Realm_Name/.well-known/openid-configuration`
- RHBK servers without /auth context path: `https://rhbk.example.com:8443/realms/Realm_Name`
- JWKS endpoint: `https://rhbk.example.com:8443/realms/Realm_Name/protocol/openid-connect/certs`

**Integration pattern** (unverified)
- Point FastAPI OAuth configuration at Keycloak realm discovery endpoint
- Retrieve public keys to verify JWTs in middleware
- Use scopes or roles inside tokens for access control
- Use PyJWKClient to retrieve public key from Keycloak's keystore
- Verify JWT authenticity using RS256 algorithm via jwt.decode
- Common pattern: pydantic BaseSettings class to centralize Keycloak endpoints (openid-configuration, JWKS, token URL)
- Async JWKS fetcher with caching

#### Azure AD Integration

**fastapi-azure-auth library** (unverified)
- Implements Azure Entra ID and Azure Entra ID B2C authentication and authorization for FastAPI APIs
- Supports single-tenant, multi-tenant, and B2C scenarios
- Version 5.2.0 released July 25, 2024
- Main feature in 5.2.0: customizable scheme names for OpenAPI documentation
- Python 3.8+ required
- Installation: `pip install fastapi-azure-auth` or `poetry add fastapi-azure-auth`

**Multi-tenant features** (unverified)
- MultiTenantAzureAuthorizationCodeBearer class enables authentication from any Azure Entra ID tenant
- Uses /common OpenID endpoint
- Issuer validation is primary mechanism for controlling which tenants can authenticate
- JWT iss (issuer) claim contains tenant ID for validation against whitelist
- iss_callable function invoked during token validation when enabled
- IssuerFetcher pattern maintains in-memory cache of allowed tenant IDs to issuer URLs
- Cache refresh every hour
- tid claim (Tenant ID) can be validated against pre-selected tenants
- validate_iss parameter can be set to True/False to control issuer validation

**Authentication scheme classes** (unverified)
- SingleTenantAzureAuthorizationCodeBearer for single-tenant apps
- MultiTenantAzureAuthorizationCodeBearer for multi-tenant apps
- B2CMultiTenantAuthorizationCodeBearer for Azure AD B2C apps

**fastapi-microsoft-identity alternative** (unverified)
- requires_auth decorator checks JWT Access Token validity
- Raises AuthError (HTTP 401) if token is invalid
- Available on PyPI: https://pypi.org/project/fastapi-microsoft-identity/

**Azure AD JWT validation** (unverified)
- Required dependencies: fastapi, httpx, python-dotenv, python-jose, msal, uvicorn
- Process: retrieve public keys from Microsoft's JWK endpoint and verify JWT token signature
- authorize dependency validates and decodes token against Azure AD App and required scopes
- Generates User instance based on token contents

#### Auth0 Integration

**auth0-fastapi-api (official SDK)** (unverified)
- Official Auth0 SDK for API authentication
- Python 3.9+ required
- Installation: `pip install auth0-fastapi-api`
- Uses Authlib for JWT verification
- require_auth(...) dependency for protecting routes
- Automatically detects and validates Bearer and DPoP authentication schemes
- Parses token, checks signature via Auth0's JWKS, validates standard claims (iss, aud, exp)
- GitHub: https://github.com/auth0/auth0-fastapi-api

**DPoP (Demonstrating Proof-of-Possession) support** (unverified)
- Validates both access token and DPoP proof
- Cryptographic binding of tokens to private keys
- Mixed mode accepts both Bearer and DPoP tokens (recommended for migration)
- DPoP-only mode rejects Bearer tokens
- Custom timing configuration: clock skew tolerance and maximum DPoP proof age
- DPoP currently in Early Access (requires Auth0 support to enable)
- RFC 9449 compliance with ES256 signature validation
- Clients must include both Authorization: DPoP <token> and DPoP: <proof> headers

**auth0-api-python (framework-agnostic)** (unverified)
- Python SDK for securing APIs with Auth0 access tokens
- Supports Bearer & DPoP authentication schemes
- OIDC discovery, JWT validation
- Framework-agnostic integration (FastAPI, Django, Flask)
- verify_request() method automatically detects and validates Bearer or DPoP schemes
- Flexible configuration with "Allowed" and "Required" DPoP modes
- GitHub: https://github.com/auth0/auth0-api-python

**auth0-fastapi (web app SDK)** (unverified)
- For web applications with session-based authentication
- get_session() method passed through Depends
- PyPI: https://pypi.org/project/auth0-fastapi/

**fastapi-auth0 (community library)** (unverified)
- Integrate FastAPI with https://auth0.com
- Automatic Swagger UI support for implicit scheme
- Social provider sign-in with no additional code
- PyPI: https://pypi.org/project/fastapi-auth0/

